<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ptolemy VIII Physcon</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 182–116 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/2nd-century-bce">2nd century BCE</a> · Also known as Ptolemy VIII Euergetes II</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ptolemy VIII, nicknamed Physcon, was a Ptolemaic king who quarrelled for decades with his brother Ptolemy VI. In 163 BCE <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> settled the dispute by giving him <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyrenaica">Cyrenaica</a> as a separate kingdom. After his brother's death in 145 BCE he became king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>, reigning until 116 BCE amid conflict with his sister and wife Cleopatra II.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ptolemy-viii-physcon.jpg" alt="Ptolemy VIII Physcon" width="320" height="403" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Yale · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Head_of_Ptolemy_VIII.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
